    'The counts that decide who is drawn are now counts of articles (`research/nv8_articles.tsv`, `scripts/as_built/nv8_articles.py`): the 1,086 pages of the first search and the 173 saved since are 1,201 articles once copies of one article are joined (the same address, or four fifths of the shorter text inside the longer), and 1,134 are counted. A page is not counted when its own date, read as a U.S. Eastern day, is after Nov 12 (44 pages) or before Oct 29 (12, background pages), when no text could be read (9) or when it is not a news piece (7). The date is the page\'s own stamp; where the header carries none it is read from the page\'s address or its stamp line, and the table gives the words it was read from (`scripts/as_built/nv8_page_dates.py`). Two mistakes of the first version of this table were found before anything was released: it compared dates as text, so that stamps such as "Nov 12th 2026" or a time in an Asian zone read as later than Nov 12, and it counted hand-saved pages whose header carries no date, 25 of them dated Nov 13 or 14.',
    'Three members of Congress were added, each named in three or more counted articles for something said or done on the matter: Sen. Tim Scott (his letters of Nov 12 asking Huang and Lutnick to testify before Senate Banking), Sen. Pete Ricketts (his statement of Nov 9, and remarks of Nov 10 and Nov 12) and Rep. Richard Neal (the letter of Nov 12 with Sen. Wyden). Each has the same lines of record as the other members (rows TY146 to TY163, built by the same script; AnthroPAC\'s $2,000 to Ricketts is drawn as row MT60, so its member line TY152 is not drawn twice). The figure now draws 27 members; all 24 drawn before stay at three or more.',
