    'The 31 analysts and experts and the 124 bylines that the pages saved since added were looked up on Nov 15 in the 85 tables of the four evidence sets by a reader from another model family (after seven controls), and again by the whole-name search. One has a tie of his own on record and is drawn (Joshua Hodges, a commissioner quoted by CNN, whom Anthropic named to its advisory council in Aug 2025; row MT61; the commission\'s page and Anthropic\'s announcement give the same earlier post). Not drawn, each with a written reason: one whose group has grants on record from an investor in Anthropic, which is outside the rule applied to every analyst; one at a university whose only award names another project; one whose name matches a person in the tables with nothing to tie the two; one analyst at a bank among the lenders. No byline has a record; for one the tables hold an officer, of the same name, of a hedge fund named Anthropic Capital Fund, whose affiliation with the company is not established, and nothing ties the officer to the reporter.',
