    'The figure\'s rule as written draws a report of an earlier act on the day of the first page that carries it. Applied to all of these it would about double the number of chips. Whether the image should carry them all, or carry acts and new reporting of the fifteen days and leave recalled background to a table and the interactive map, '
    'is a question of the figure\'s scope that is its owner\'s to decide. Until it is decided no open line is drawn on purpose. That is not the same as none being on a chip: three readings and the builder\'s search have found lines counted as open whose act a chip words, whole (now marked carried; the next list counts them) or in part (twenty-three acts, now marked so), and the check behind this sentence is a search by words, not a reading of every line against every chip. The reports of earlier acts drawn in the last three answers stay drawn.',
    'Limits. The readers were given the chips and the tie lines, not the members\' lines or the figure\'s boxes, so some of their candidates are carried there (the builder checked those about Anthropic, not the rest). The readers\' verdict "carried" was not read again except where a page is earlier than the chip. '
