    "The take-in's table and text. Four dispositions are amended in a new column of the table, which keeps what the take-in decided beside what stands now: the senator's request and the roadshow are parts of chips; a statement in the New York Post's report is carried by the chip that gives that report and is not shown to be a relay of an earlier response; and one of the 43 records of no reply says only that the White House did not comment, with no request stated. The text no longer calls all 43 requests that went unanswered. The reading could not trace the sentence about an outlet's analysis that the controversy is a blip for the two companies: it came from the builder's sessions' reading of a counted page, not from a group, and the list of the take-in now names the page and says so.",
